1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,146
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03,196 --> 00:00:05,865
AI for Teens, video 6.

3
00:00:05,915 --> 00:00:09,820
Bias: find it, fix what you can.

4
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:15,420
Bias often enters through who appears in the data — and who does not.

5
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:21,800
A face dataset from one city and age group will fail elsewhere.

6
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:27,062
A resume screener trained only on past hires from one college can

7
00:00:27,112 --> 00:00:28,600
automate past bias.

8
00:00:29,950 --> 00:00:35,918
Safer directions include handwriting samples across many schools and scripts, and plant

9
00:00:35,968 --> 00:00:39,100
disease photos in several lighting conditions.

10
00:00:40,450 --> 00:00:46,288
Collect more varied data, measure errors by group, involve affected users, and

11
00:00:46,338 --> 00:00:49,610
sometimes decide not to automate a decision.

12
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:52,397
Let us recap.

13
00:00:52,447 --> 00:00:56,129
Missing groups create biased models.

14
00:00:56,179 --> 00:01:00,274
Measurement by group makes harm visible.

15
00:01:00,324 --> 00:01:04,420
Next: Generative AI: useful, not oracle.
